The data file t200101.iea contains 18 columms of data which are listed below.
The measurements were carried out on January 20 1993 for the turbine in normal operation.

Inflow was measured with a five hole pitot tube at radius 6.83 m and blade segment forces were measured at three
stations, R1=3.555, R2=6.475, R3=9.275. 

For derivation of the coefficients CN and CT at the different radial stations, the following velocties were used:

V1=Vmeasured*(3.555/6.83)
V2=Vmeasured*(6.475/6.83)
V3=Vmeasured*(9.275/6.83)

V2 is the velocity contained in the data file.

The angle of attack is the measured angle in radius 6.83 relative to the chord but subtracted
a constant 4.7 deg. in order to get coincidence between the measured power curve as function of
angle of attack and the same curve computed with the BEM method.

The scan frequency is 25 hz and all the data have been passed through a digital low pass band filter with a 
cut off frequence between 3 and 3.5 hz.

NOTE:

The calibration of Flap1 and Flap2 is uncertain in the present data file.

 
  
Channel   Variable description                 Label         Units

     1      Time                                 t             sec
     2      Air Pressure                         p-a           mbar
     3      Temperature                          T             deg. 
     4      Wind speed                           Vw            m/s
     5      Wind direction                       phi-y         deg.

     6      Rotor azimuth                        phi-r         deg.
     7      Rotor speed                          omega         rpm.
     8      Electrical power                     Pow.          kW.
     9      Flap1 (flap moment blade 1)          Flap1         kNm.
    10      Flap2 (flap moment blade 2)          Flap2         kNm.

    11      Flap3 (flap moment blade 3)          Flap3         kNm.
    12      Normal coefficient seg. 1            CN1   
    13      Normal coefficient seg. 2            CN2
    14      Tangential coefficient seg. 2        CT2
    15      Normal coefficient seg. 3            CN3

    16      Tangential coefficient seg. 3        CT3
    17      Measured angle of attack             alpha         deg.
    18      Measured inflow velocity             V2           m/s

Note Gerard Schepers: The number of records is 14913; 
Record 1 is  header
Record 2 is mean value
Record 3 is standard deviation
Record 4 is min-value
Record 5 is max-value
Data start at record 6.
The measurement period is 596.3 seconds
